  "id": "Compound::DB00492 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Fosinopril, a commonly prescribed antihypertensive drug, is shown to bind to Slc15a1, a protein involved in the transport of oligopeptides and peptides in a proton-dependent manner. This binding is linked to the participation of Slc15a1 in multiple transport activities, including the peptide/proton symporter activity and the oligopeptide transporter activity. These activities are ultimately associated with Slc15a2, suggesting a potential functional relationship between Fosinopril and Slc15a2. The evidence indicates that Fosinopril may influence Slc15a1, which in turn modulates the activity of Slc15a2 through shared functional pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Fosinopril could affect Slc15a2, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a strong and consistent relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct functional link between Fosinopril and Slc15a2.",
